			<div class="content" id="post-content-3869145">
									

<p>Seconding Safe Classification.</p>
<p>Locking the door in a box (and the objects associated with it) effectively contains it.</p>
<p>Even if Vogel had some kind of conceptual contamination (rather than hubris) that was due to exposure to the SCP/what he read, this contamination can still be safely boxed.</p>
<p>It definatly <em>wants</em> to get out/let more people in. But it hasn't really been shown to be able to exert it's influence onto our world so long as the door is closed and nothing goes in or out.</p>
<p>Sapient SCPs are usually Euclid, but this thing is basicaly a djinn. It can only act with sapient-agency if you let it out of the bottle. Otherwise it's just a dangerous bottle (door)</p>

