					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crow-cat" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3952131); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3952131&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606920952" alt="Crow-Cat" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3952131)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crow-cat" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3952131); return false;" >Crow-Cat</a></span> <span class="odate time_1548093622 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Jan 2019 18:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4126328">
									

<p>I&#8230; like this. But there are some things which prevent me from upvoting.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Review</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Review</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First things first, I agree with the other commenters that the paragraph describing what SCP-3608 <em>is</em> should be the first thing in the description. &quot;Sapient, predatory dimension located behind a blue door,&quot; is a really good hook that's made even more effective by the SCProcs being so short! I seriously recommend switching the paragraphs around in the description.</p>
<p>I'd have to say that the police interview was my favorite log in the article. The officer actually seemed like a real character and not just a medium for exposition. It's a very well written dialogue about a normal guy encountering something weird and other worldly. The one thing I'm confused about is when he describes the structure as &quot;five meters deep.&quot; What does that mean?</p>
<p>In the first expedition the D-Class is described as going inside 3608-1, but 3608-1 is described as being identical to the structure the officer encountered, who said it didn't have any doors or windows. Shouldn't the log specify that it has doors now?<br />
Other than that, I think the four expedition logs are really good. I especially like how they show SCP-3608 slowly learning and adapting.</p>
<p>The interview with the D-Class and the recovered materials log were pretty good too; the brutality and reach of SCP-3608's abilities respectively.</p>
<p>I really don't like operation lockout. It doesn't make sense for the Foundation to try destroying an anomaly that hasn't been exceptionally dangerous to them, humanity, or containment. I'd recommend removing it altogether.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I really don't understand why Dr. Vogel would believe</span><br />
After thinking about it, I think I'm <em>kinda</em> okay with what Dr. Vogel does. He was being manipulated by an entity that can change your emotions, and it stands to reason his thoughts were influenced by his feelings. But, I don't understand why he wasn't screened for possible memetic contamination after reading the notebook, or at the very least have a background check on him given the strange message it gave him.<br />
Powers killing himself after he shoots Vogel seems&#8230; overdramatic and WAY too big of a leap.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Review</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>TL;DR It starts out good but goes downhill after 3608-R. Novote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
